Annotations: |
  This cell is the top-level client boundary of the network/protocol library: the app module
  talks to the Signal service exclusively through the types declared here, never through the
  library's internal internal.* packages directly. Sending, receiving, and account management
  are split into three separate client classes rather than one god object.

---

"SignalServiceMessageSender(pushServiceSocket: PushServiceSocket, store: SignalServiceDataStore, sessionLock: SignalSessionLock, messageApi: MessageApi, keysApi: KeysApi)":
  location: SignalServiceMessageSender.java
  annotations: |
    The outbound client: encrypts and transmits messages, receipts, and sync messages to one or
    more recipients.

    `pushServiceSocket`: low-level authenticated transport.
    `store`: the multi-account protocol/session store this sender encrypts against.
    `sessionLock`: serializes encrypt/decrypt operations against `store` across threads.
    `messageApi`, `keysApi`: typed REST clients for message submission and prekey lookups.
  methods:
    "sendDataMessage(recipient: SignalServiceAddress, contentHint: ContentHint, message: SignalServiceDataMessage, urgent: Boolean, includePniSignature: Boolean) -> result:SendMessageResult": |
      Encrypts and sends `message` to a single recipient.

      `recipient`: the message's destination.
      `contentHint`: how a recipient that fails to decrypt should react (e.g. request a resend).
      `urgent`: whether delivery should bypass battery-saving deferral where the transport
      supports it.
    "sendGroupDataMessage(distributionId: DistributionId, recipients: List<SignalServiceAddress>, isRecipientUpdate: Boolean, contentHint: ContentHint, message: SignalServiceDataMessage, urgent: Boolean, isForStory: Boolean) -> results:List<SendMessageResult>": |
      Encrypts `message` once per sender-key distribution and sends it to every address in
      recipients.

      `distributionId`: identifies which sender-key distribution to encrypt under.
      recipients: the group's current member addresses.
    "sendReceipt(recipient: SignalServiceAddress, message: SignalServiceReceiptMessage, includePniSignature: Boolean) -> result:SendMessageResult": |
      Sends a delivery or read receipt to `recipient` for a previously-received message.
    "sendSyncMessage(message: SignalServiceSyncMessage) -> result:SendMessageResult": |
      Sends a message to the local user's other linked devices (e.g. "I read this on another
      device"), never to another person.

"SignalServiceMessageReceiver(socket: PushServiceSocket)":
  location: SignalServiceMessageReceiver.java
  annotations: |
    The inbound/attachment-retrieval client: downloads and decrypts attachments, avatars,
    stickers, and backup files that a SignalServiceDataMessage only references by pointer.

    `socket`: low-level authenticated transport used for all retrieval calls.
  methods:
    "retrieveAttachment(pointer: SignalServiceAttachmentPointer, destination: File, maxSizeBytes: Long, integrityCheck: IntegrityCheck) -> stream:InputStream": |
      Downloads the attachment referenced by `pointer` to `destination` and returns a stream of
      its decrypted plaintext contents.

      `pointer`: attachment reference received inside a SignalServiceDataMessage.
      `destination`: local file the (still-encrypted) download is written to; if it already
      exists, the download resumes from it.
      `integrityCheck`: expected digest/plaintext hash used to verify the download.
    "retrieveProfileAvatar(path: String, destination: File, profileKey: ProfileKey, maxSizeBytes: Long) -> stream:InputStream": |
      Downloads and decrypts a profile avatar image.
    "retrieveSticker(packId: ByteArray, packKey: ByteArray, stickerId: Int) -> data:ByteArray": |
      Downloads and decrypts a single sticker's image data.
    "retrieveStickerManifest(packId: ByteArray, packKey: ByteArray) -> manifest:SignalServiceStickerManifest": |
      Downloads, decrypts, and parses the manifest (title, author, cover, sticker list) for a
      sticker pack.

"SignalServiceAccountManager()":
  location: SignalServiceAccountManager.java
  annotations: |
    The account registration/management client: everything about creating, verifying, and
    administering the account itself, as opposed to sending/receiving messages once
    registered. Constructed either with static credentials (createWithStaticCredentials) for
    pre-registration flows, or with an authenticated websocket for an already-registered account.
  methods:
    "getGroupsV2Api() -> api:GroupsV2Api": |
      A client for group-v2-specific server operations, scoped to this account's credentials.
    "getRegistrationApi() -> api:RegistrationApi": |
      A client for the registration-session server operations.
    "getSecureValueRecoveryV2(mrEnclave: String) -> svr:SecureValueRecoveryV2": |
      A client for backing up/restoring the account's PIN-derived master key to/from the given
      secure-value-recovery enclave.
    "getWhoAmI() -> response:WhoAmIResponse": |
      Asks the server to identify the account these credentials belong to.
    "requestRegistrationPushChallenge(sessionId: String, gcmRegistrationId: String)": |
      Asks the server to push a challenge value to the given FCM registration id, which can then
      be submitted to bypass a CAPTCHA requirement for the given registration session.
    "checkNetworkConnection()": |
      Pings the storage service as a lightweight connectivity check.
    "cancelInFlightRequests()": |
      Cancels any requests this manager's underlying transport currently has in flight.

"SignalServiceDataStore()":
  location: SignalServiceDataStore.java
  annotations: |
    Resolves the per-account protocol store to use for a given identity, for apps (like this one)
    that manage both an ACI and a PNI identity for the same local user.
  methods:
    "get(accountIdentifier: ServiceId) -> store:SignalServiceAccountDataStore": |
      The account-scoped store for the given service identifier.
    "aci() -> store:SignalServiceAccountDataStore": |
      The store for the local user's ACI identity.
    "pni() -> store:SignalServiceAccountDataStore": |
      The store for the local user's PNI identity. Throws if the account has no PNI.
    "isMultiDevice() -> multiDevice:Boolean": |
      Whether the local account currently has any linked devices.

"SignalServiceAccountDataStore()":
  location: SignalServiceAccountDataStore.java
  annotations: |
    Extends the underlying libsignal protocol store contract (session/prekey/identity/sender-key
    state) with the additional bookkeeping the service layer needs but the protocol layer itself
    does not: multi-device awareness.
  methods:
    "isMultiDevice() -> multiDevice:Boolean": |
      Whether the account this store belongs to currently has linked devices.
    "setMultiDevice(isMultiDevice: Boolean)": |
      Updates the store's record of whether the account has linked devices.

"SignalSessionLock()":
  location: SignalSessionLock.java
  annotations: |
    Injectable lock abstraction so that encrypt/decrypt operations against a
    `SignalServiceAccountDataStore` can be made thread-safe without this library dictating a
    specific locking implementation.
  methods:
    "acquire() -> lock:Lock": |
      Blocks until the lock is available, then returns a Closeable handle representing
      ownership; the caller releases the lock by closing it.

